+// One conversation: its chat page and the tabs that show it. Most chats
+// belong to the one tab they were opened on. A chat follows its agent task to
+// the tabs the agent brings forward or works in, and the two tabs of a split
+// view share one, so a chat can belong to several tabs, but the panel shows
+// it beside one tab at a time.
+//
+// The chat owns its page rather than a view: the side panel deletes the views
+// of entries it closes or no longer needs, and a reply or a task must carry
+// on while its tab is in the background. Each tab that shows the chat holds a
+// reference, as does the view showing it, and the chat ends when the last one
+// goes: when the user closes it on its last tab, when its last tab closes, or
+// when AI turns off.
+class AssistantChat : public base::RefCounted<AssistantChat>,
